# getInfo User Presence Check
# Emulate USB authenticator "flashing button" user presence for authenticatorGetInfo.
# When a getInfo request arrives, prompt the user (yes/no) before returning the response.
# Timeout after 15 seconds. Bring app to foreground if it is not already there.

---

## Context

Request flow:
  BLE write
    -> HIDPasskey.onOutputReport()          [app/src/main/java/com/isfs/blekey/hidsvc/HIDPasskey.java:77]
    -> CtapHid.processMessage()             [lib/src/com/isfs/blekey/ctap/CtapHid.java:268]
    -> CtapHid.cbor()                       [lib/src/com/isfs/blekey/ctap/CtapHid.java:394]
    -> AuthenticatorAPI.process()           [lib/src/com/isfs/blekey/authenticator/AuthenticatorAPI.java:1025]
    -> AuthenticatorAPI.getInfo()           [lib/src/com/isfs/blekey/authenticator/AuthenticatorAPI.java:904]

The pipeline is currently synchronous. getInfo() builds and returns the response immediately.
The response is queued back to the BLE host via HIDPasskey -> HIDService.addInputReport().

Relevant CTAP2 status codes (Ctap2StatusCode.java):
  USER_ACTION_TIMEOUT  0x2F  -- user did not respond within 15 seconds
  OPERATION_DENIED     0x27  -- user tapped No
  OPERATION_DENIED     0x27  -- no callback registered (fallback)

Existing notification infrastructure:
  ForegroundNotificationService.CHANNEL_ID = "FIDO2_NOTIFICATION_CHANNEL"  (IMPORTANCE_HIGH)
  POST_NOTIFICATIONS permission already declared in AndroidManifest.xml

---

## Tasks

### STEP 1 — AuthenticatorAPI: add UserPresenceCallback interface
File: lib/src/com/isfs/blekey/authenticator/AuthenticatorAPI.java

[ ] Add a public static inner interface UserPresenceCallback with three methods:
      void onApproved(byte[] getInfoResponse);
      void onDenied();
      void onTimeout();

[ ] Add a private static field:
      private static UserPresenceCallback userPresenceCallback = null;

[ ] Add a public static setter:
      public static void setUserPresenceCallback(UserPresenceCallback cb)

[ ] Modify getInfo() (line 904) to:
    - Build the CBOR info map and call success(Cbor.encode(info)) as before, storing result in a local variable.
    - If userPresenceCallback == null, return error(Ctap2StatusCode.OPERATION_DENIED).
    - Otherwise call userPresenceCallback.onApproved(response) and return null.
      (null signals to the caller that the response will be delivered asynchronously.)

    NOTE: error() and success() are private static helpers already in this class (lines 275, 285).


### STEP 2 — CtapHid: handle null (deferred) response from process()
File: lib/src/com/isfs/blekey/ctap/CtapHid.java

[ ] In cbor() (line 394), after calling AuthenticatorAPI.process():
    - If the return value is null, do NOT call buildCborInitAndSequencePackets().
    - Do NOT set this.responseReady = true.
    - Store a reference to `this` CtapHid instance in a static pending map keyed by CID,
      so the deferred response can be injected later.
      Suggested: private static Map<byte[], CtapHid> pendingUserPresence = new HashMap<>();

[ ] Add a public method to inject a deferred CBOR response:
      public void injectDeferredResponse(byte[] cborResponse) throws IOException {
          buildCborInitAndSequencePackets(cborResponse);
          this.responseReady = true;
      }

[ ] Add a public static method to retrieve and remove a pending instance by CID:
      public static CtapHid takePendingUserPresence(byte[] cid)


### STEP 3 — HIDPasskey: add sendDeferredResponse helper
File: app/src/main/java/com/isfs/blekey/hidsvc/HIDPasskey.java

[ ] Add a method:
      public void sendDeferredResponse(byte[] cid, byte[] cborResponse)
    - Calls CtapHid.takePendingUserPresence(cid) to retrieve the pending CtapHid instance.
    - Calls cmd.injectDeferredResponse(cborResponse) on it.
    - Drains cmd.hasMoreResponses() / cmd.getResponseSegment() and calls
      this._service.addInputReport(frame) for each segment, same as onOutputReport() does.

[ ] Store the last seen CID so the deferred callback can pass it to sendDeferredResponse.
    The CID is available in onOutputReport() from the parsed report bytes (bytes 0-3).
    Add a field: private byte[] lastCid;
    Set it in onOutputReport() after parsing the CID.


### STEP 4 — ServerActivity: register callback and show user presence UI
File: app/src/main/java/com/isfs/blekey/activity/ServerActivity.java

[ ] Add a field:
      private byte[] pendingGetInfoCid = null;
      private byte[] pendingGetInfoResponse = null;
      private Handler uiHandler = new Handler(Looper.getMainLooper());
      private Runnable timeoutRunnable = null;
      private AlertDialog userPresenceDialog = null;

[ ] In setupPasskeyPeripheralProvider(), after creating passkeyService, register the callback:
      AuthenticatorAPI.setUserPresenceCallback(new AuthenticatorAPI.UserPresenceCallback() {
          public void onApproved(byte[] getInfoResponse) {
              pendingGetInfoCid = passkeyService.getLastCid();   // see Step 3
              pendingGetInfoResponse = getInfoResponse;
              uiHandler.post(() -> showUserPresencePrompt());
          }
          public void onDenied() { /* not called from API, only from UI */ }
          public void onTimeout() { /* not called from API, only from UI */ }
      });

[ ] Add showUserPresencePrompt():
    - If the app is in the foreground (see foreground detection below), show an AlertDialog:
        Title: "Authentication Request"
        Message: "A device is requesting authenticator info. Allow?"
        Positive button: "Allow"  -> calls deliverGetInfoApproved()
        Negative button: "Deny"   -> calls deliverGetInfoDenied()
    - If the app is NOT in the foreground, fire a notification (see Step 5) and store
      the pending response; show the dialog in onResume() / onNewIntent().

[ ] Add deliverGetInfoApproved():
    - Cancel the timeout runnable.
    - Call passkeyService.getHIDPasskey().sendDeferredResponse(pendingGetInfoCid, pendingGetInfoResponse).
    - Clear pendingGetInfoCid and pendingGetInfoResponse.

[ ] Add deliverGetInfoDenied():
    - Cancel the timeout runnable.
    - Call passkeyService.getHIDPasskey().sendDeferredResponse(
          pendingGetInfoCid,
          AuthenticatorAPI.buildErrorResponse(Ctap2StatusCode.OPERATION_DENIED)).
      NOTE: buildErrorResponse() is a new public static helper to add to AuthenticatorAPI (see Step 1 note).
    - Clear pending fields.

[ ] Add 15-second timeout:
    - Start a Handler.postDelayed(timeoutRunnable, 15_000) when showUserPresencePrompt() is called.
    - timeoutRunnable dismisses the dialog (if showing) and calls deliverGetInfoTimeout().

[ ] Add deliverGetInfoTimeout():
    - Dismiss dialog if showing.
    - Call passkeyService.getHIDPasskey().sendDeferredResponse(
          pendingGetInfoCid,
          AuthenticatorAPI.buildErrorResponse(Ctap2StatusCode.USER_ACTION_TIMEOUT)).
    - Clear pending fields.

[ ] Foreground detection:
    - Add a boolean field: private boolean isInForeground = false;
    - Set true in onResume(), false in onPause().

[ ] Handle bring-to-front in onResume() / onNewIntent():
    - If pendingGetInfoResponse != null and isInForeground, call showUserPresencePrompt().

[ ] In onDestroy(), clear the AuthenticatorAPI callback:
      AuthenticatorAPI.setUserPresenceCallback(null);
    Also cancel any pending timeout runnable and dismiss any open dialog.


